message.content:
Looking at the functional results (8/8 passed) and the bounded status violation at S7, position 2, the issue is likely that `status` is not being explicitly reset to `16#0000` on the no-error path. In CODESYS, outputs retain their previous values between calls, so if `status` was set to an error code on a previous scan, it would remain even after the error condition clears.

Let me apply the fix:

```json
{
  "edits": [
    {
      "old": "    error       : BOOL := FALSE;
    status      : WORD := 16#0000;",
      "new": "    error       : BOOL := FALSE;
    status      : WORD := 16#0000;
    tmp_statusSet : BOOL := FALSE;"
    },
    {
      "old": "IF loLevel >= hiLevel THEN
    error := TRUE;
    status := 16#8001;
    RETURN;
END_IF;

// Parameter validation: hystWindow must be less than the range between hiLevel and loLevel
IF hystWindow >= (hiLevel - loLevel) THEN
    error := TRUE;
    status := 16#8002;
    RETURN;
END_IF;

// High alarm: trigger when Value exceeds hiLevel, clear when below hiLevel minus hysteresis",
      "new": "// Error checks and status assignment
IF loLevel >= hiLevel THEN
    error := TRUE;
    status := 16#8001;
    RETURN;
END_IF;

// Parameter validation: hystWindow must be less than the range between hiLevel and loLevel
IF hystWindow >= (hiLevel - loLevel) THEN
    error := TRUE;
    status := 16#8002;
    RETURN;
END_IF;

// No error - explicitly reset status and error outputs
error := FALSE;
status := 16#0000;

// High alarm: trigger when Value exceeds hiLevel, clear when below hiLevel minus hysteresis"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Fix explanation:** The bounded status violation occurs because `status` was not being explicitly reset when error conditions cleared. In CODESYS, output variables retain their values between FB calls. The edit adds an explicit `status := 16#0000` and `error := FALSE` assignment on the no-error path to ensure the status remains bounded to the expected value after any previous error is resolved.
